    "notes": "Fix of KG-2026-11-22-b, same story and score. QA fail was one shot of 5.3 s: the cake delivery map held a silenceBefore, an ellipsis and two lines. Now that map shot carries only Shruti's line (no ellipsis) and Ruhi's \"Haaw! Host bhi late!\" moves to its own living-room reaction shot with Tanya sweating; the rasmalai map shot is split the same way so Tanya answers from the living room. 13 shots, every shot one or two short lines with hold 0.1, one silenceBefore, one silent map shot of 1.4 s, pace 27. Real kitty scene: the late fine rule plus the late friend sharing her live location. One want (Tanya wants the fine money, then the cake from it), one game (each map stop pushes the meter), played ordinary (still at home, lift excuse), ordinary (baraat jam in shaadi season), absurd (she stops to buy rasmalai to get the fine waived, which costs her another Rs 150). Claim before reveal: Tanya celebrates the free cake twice before the delivery map shows she ordered it at 4:45. Twist is a see-it delivery map chip. Button mirrors the hook: Avika says Tanya's exact rule back and Shruti repeats Meter chalu!, so it loops into the start; Tanya using Avika's Bas paanch minute line is the kicker. Pipeline: every two-line shot is 8 words or fewer with hold 0.1, one silenceBefore, one silent shot of 1.4 s, pace 27. Endings tried: Avika pays in rasmalai (no flip); the cake boy rings and Tanya pays him (flip unclear muted); kept the meter turning on the host. Lead is Avika (last reel Shruti). Kind humour: nobody is mocked, the fine is a game."
